RF.put("questb:b62",{"8702":{"id":8702,"t":"Ring of Unspoken Names","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ceremonial Ring, 2 Jasper Idols, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ceremonial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Jasper Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of Unspoken Names\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8622":{"id":8622,"t":"Stormcaller's Hauberk","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nCarapace of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nStormcaller's Hauberk\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Horde Class Shaman Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8622\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Stormcaller's Hauberk this quest\nBring the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8542":{"id":8542,"t":"The Horde Needs Tin Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 54.","obj":"Bring 20 Tin Bars to Grunt Maug at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Tin Bar","desc":"Lok'tar, ‹race›, I'm sure you already know that we're going to war at Ahn'Qiraj with the insects. But first the Warchief has decided that we're going to do something called 'prepare'. Though I'd rather be sharpening weapons and hammering armor into shape, I'm proud to have been chosen to be in charge of tin bar collection here. But I cannot do that without your help.\nSo I need you to go out and make tin bars and bring them back to me here. I think I'm going to need more than I can count.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"The dredge strikers are a serious threat and must be dealt with quickly!","done":"You have my sincere gratitude. Your efforts in helping Cenarion Hold have shown true courage.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.1,"y":65,"n":"Grunt Maug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6942":{"id":6942,"t":"Call of Air - Slidore's Fleet","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Soldier's Medal Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl , Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Winterax Berserker and 4 more","back":"My gryphons are poised to strike at the front lines but cannot make the attack until the lines are thinned out.\nThe Frostwolf warriors charged with holding the front lines wear medals of service proudly upon their chests. Rip those medals off their rotten corpses and bring them back here.\nOnce the front line is sufficiently thinned out, I will make the call to air! Death from above!","done":"Keep em coming, soldier! The Aerie gryphons will be ready to strike in no time at all!\nStart Wing Commander Slidore Alterac Valley End Wing Commander Slidore Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6942","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7102":{"id":7102,"t":"Towers and Bunkers","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Destroy the banner at an enemy tower or bunker, then return to Sergeant Durgen Stormpike in the Alterac Mountains.\nBanner Destroyed","desc":"Towers and bunkers are key defensive positions, and so we must hold as many as possible! I want you to attack a tower or a bunker in Alterac Valley.\nTo do that, enter a tower with a Horde banner atop it. You will see another enemy banner inside. Pull out that banner, and a white Alliance banner will appear in its place. Well done!\nAt that point your mission for me will be complete, but hold the area long enough, and if the Horde doesn't take it back, then it will be destroyed!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You haven't yet assaulted a tower, ‹name›! What are you waiting for?","done":"I received a field report stating you helped secure an enemy banner. Well done, ‹name›! With their ranged troops out of position we can move the line of battle forward!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":36.8,"y":77.2,"n":"Sergeant Durgen Stormpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6862":{"id":6862,"t":"Zinfizzlex's Portable Shredder Unit","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"null\n30 Thorium Bar\n50 Mithril Bar\n75 Iron Bar\nSteamsaw Alterac Ram in Alterac Valley , Frostwolf Warrior , Stormpike Guardsman in Alterac Valley , Commander Karl Philips in Alterac Valley and 1 more","desc":"null","rew":"You will receive:\nZinfizzlex's Portable Shredder Unit\n+25 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I'm as anxious as you are to try out my portable shredder unit, ‹race›, but before I can make the kit, I'm going to need materials - lots of materials!\nTo be exact, I'm going to need a mountain of thorium, mithril, and iron. I will also need one steamsaw per unit. You'll have to get those at the lumber mill.\nWhen I was nosing around in here (before my capture) I noticed a pile of steamsaws at the Stormpike lumber camp.\nMaster Engineer Zinfizzlex wants you to bring him the following:\nStart Master Engineer Zinfizzlex End Master Engineer Zinfizzlex Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6862","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"702":{"id":702,"t":"Guile of the Raptor","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Tor'gan's Orb to Gor'mul.\nTor'gan's Orb\nProvided: Tor'gan's Orb","desc":"Take this orb and use its energy to give Gor'mul the essence of the raptor. Surely this will invigorate his spirit and give him new purpose in life. With him returned to normal, we can explain to him the current state of the Horde, and we will have a great warrior's assistance in our unceasing battles.","rew":"Experience: 290\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Returned again have you? Indeed there is nothing more I could wish for now than more of Tor'gan's pity.\nWhat have you for me this time? Perhaps a piece of brightly colored string? Or a length of rope to end this misery of mine...","done":"At least it is something interesting you bring to me this time. A strange power it emits...","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":72.6,"y":33.9,"n":"Gor'mul","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6462":{"id":6462,"t":"Troll Charm","lv":24,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Troll Charms to Mitsuwa at the Zoram'gar Outpost.\n8 Troll Charm Troll Chest","desc":"My kinfolk were traveling here with many sacred troll charms, but the Thistlefur furbolgs attacked and killed them before they reached Zoram'gar! Those vile Furbolgs!\nI miss my brothers and sisters who were killed, but we will meet again in the afterlife. However, their troll charms hold great value in this world. It is an outrage that the furbolgs have them!\n‹name›, you must retrieve the charms! They are in chests in Thistlefur Hold, a cave at the end of Thistlefur Village, north of Astranaar.","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Did you find the charms, ‹name›? Every moment the furbolgs possess those sacred items, my blood boils with rage!","done":"You found them! Thank you! Thank you, ‹name›! You do not know how great a thing you have done for me.\nA troll without his charm is like an orc without his battle scars...\nWorthless.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.9,"n":"Mitsuwa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1022":{"id":1022,"t":"The Howling Vale","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Howling Vale and study the Tome of Mel'Thandris, then return to Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow at Forest Song.\nView the Tome of Mel'Thandris","desc":"Though we have put many resources and much effort into driving the remaining demons from the Felwood to the north, our successes have been few. We have been able to keep much of the demonic presence from Ashenvale.\nTo the north, near the Felwood border, the ruined shrine of Mel'Thandris has been overtaken by mysterious wolf-men. Their chilling calls have led the area to be known as the Howling Vale. The Tome of Mel'Thandris kept at the shrine may shed some light on why these wolf-men have come.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The tome of the shrine is a mysterious object. It is not a book in the traditional sense. The leaves of the tome were blessed by Mel'Thandris herself, and records events of import in its pages.\nIt is hard for me to explain. If you go to the shrine, you will understand.","done":"The Tome of Mel'Thandris works in strange ways. The events it records, the events it shows... No one truly understands why it does what it does.\nNonetheless, it is clear that what Priestess Starsong received--this Scythe of Elune--bears further investigation.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":22.2,"y":53,"n":"Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"782":{"id":782,"t":"Broken Alliances","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Boss Tho'grun and bring the Sign of the Earth to Gorn in Kargath.\nSign of the Earth Boss Tho'grun","desc":"From the Horde's alliance with the dragon Deathwing during the Second War, we know that two of his lieutenants, Blacklash and Hematus, were imprisoned within Lethlor Ravine far to the east. We must silence our depraved allies of old to restore honor to the Horde!\nWe hired Tho'grun and his band of ogre mercenaries to help us obtain the Sign of the Earth, a key needed to unlock the drakes' prison. Tho'grun betrayed us though, overwhelming us and taking it for himself. Go to Camp Boff and take it back!","rew":"Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Tho'grun's betrayal... is there any wonder why the ogres are part of the Horde no longer? I will be glad to see him dead, and the Sign of the Earth returned.\nIf you've not dispatched him yet, then waste no time going to Camp Boff. It is to the southeast of Kargath.","done":"With Tho'grun dead, his corpse picked clean by the desert winds and scavenging buzzards, the ogres will be put into disarray. Though a small victory, this will lead to a much larger one\nThe Sign of the Earth is now in our possession, and we can open the black drakes' prison in Lethlor. We shall free them from endless imprisonment, albeit to their doom!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":45.6,"n":"Gorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4062":{"id":4062,"t":"The Rise of the Machines","lv":54,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Elemental Shard Sample to Lotwil Veriatus.\nYou recall Theodora saying that Lotwil was stationed in a camp to the east.\nElemental Shard Sample\nProvided: Elemental Shard Sample","desc":"G.L.A.\nThose are the 'initials' imprinted on the elemental shards. Below the initials are a rank marking of some sort. The machinations you destroyed in the Burning Steppes were of 'Rank IV.' I assume that this is a lowly rank.\nTake this shard sample to Lotwil Veriatus in the camp to the east. He is a scholar of some renown in the field of elemental sciences. He may be able to assist us in our search.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","back":"What have you got there, ‹race›?","done":"<Lotwil's face turns white.>\nI... I know these markings.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3,"y":47.8,"n":"Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"3982":{"id":3982,"t":"What Is Going On?","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,450 experience instead of 4,350, 1.25 times as much.","obj":"Defend Gor'shak.","desc":"I was sent here under the auspices of Thrall. Do you actually think these buffoons could capture me? I allowed myself to be captured so that I could gather intelligence.\n<Gor'shak whispers.>\nThe Princess of Ironforge has been kidnapped by Emperor Thaurissan. Princess Bronzebeard is in this very city! I bet old Magni's heart almost stopped when he heard that news.\n<Gor'shak laughs.>\nShhh! Do you hear that? Guards coming! DEFEND YOURSELF!","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Defend yourself, fool!","done":"That was a close call. They have been alerted to your presence... more will surely come.\nStart Commander Gor'shak End Commander Gor'shak Level 54 , requires level 48 Difficulty 48 50 52 57 Side Horde Type Dungeon Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 3982\nThe chain\n7 quests from level 52 to 60, 41,000 XP in all.\n1 [ 52 ] Disharmony of Flame\nTravel to the quarry in Blackrock Mountain and slay Overmaster Pyron.\nThunderheart Badlands\n5,100 XP\n2 [ 52 ] Commander Gor'shak\nFind Commander Gor'shak in Blackrock Depths. You recall that the crudely drawn picture of the orc included bars drawn over the portrait.\nGalamav the Marksman Badlands\n5,100 XP\n3 [ 54 ] What Is Going On? this quest\nDefend Gor'shak.\nCommander Gor'shak\n5,450 XP\n4 [ 54 ] What Is Going On?\nSpeak with Kharan Mighthammer and gather information about Princess Moira Bronzebeard's kidnapping.\nCommander Gor'shak\n6,800 XP\n5 [ 54 ] The Eastern Kingdoms\nSpeak with Thrall if you are prepared to take on the mission he has planned.\nThrall Orgrimmar\n550 XP\n6 [ 59 ] The Royal Rescue\nSlay Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and free Princess Moira Bronzebeard from his evil spell.\nThrall Orgrimmar\n8,050 XP\n7 [ 60 ] The Princess Saved?\nReturn to Thrall!\nPrincess Moira Bronzebeard\n9,950 XP","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4862":{"id":4862,"t":"En-Ay-Es-Tee-Why","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and collect 15 Spire Spider Eggs for Kibler.\nBy the sound of it, these eggs could be found near spiders.\n15 Spire Spider Egg Spire Spider Egg , Spire Spider Egg","desc":"Believe it or not, there are people out there willing to pay for the most vile of domesticated beast!\nI'd sent Bijou into the Spire to try and collect some of those spire spider eggs but I haven't heard from her in weeks. Maybe you can help me out?\nI'll tell you what, ‹name›. Go to Blackrock Spire and collect some spire spider eggs for me. Bring them back here and not only will I give you a little cash, but I'll even domesticate one for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nSmolderweb Carrier\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400","back":"Are those spider eggs in your pack or are you just happy to see me?","done":"What a load! I mean, look at all those eggs! These should bring in a right few gold.\nAs promised, here's your own little critter. Don't get bitten!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.9,"y":21.9,"n":"Kibler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5102":{"id":5102,"t":"General Drakkisath's Demise","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy General Drakkisath. Return to Marshal Maxwell when the job is done.\nGeneral Drakkisath slain","desc":"We battle against these beasts on two fronts: From our capital of Stormwind we fight them from the inside out and here, in the Burning Steppes, we take the battle to their doorstep. We must be vigilant, ‹name›. None should be spared our wrath as none of our own were spared when they struck at our homes and families.\nFind this General Drakkisath and destroy him!\nThe task certainly will not be a simple one, but the rewards shall be extravagant.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMark of Tyranny Eye of the Beast Blackhand's Breadth\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Alliance","back":"Is it done?","done":"Surely, we will strike against their dragon lords next. Well done, brave soldier of the Alliance! Well done, indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"3502":{"id":3502,"t":"One Draenei's Junk...","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Kum'isha Imperfect Draenethyst Fragments. Any form of monster in the Blasted Lands could be carrying a fragment.\nImperfect Draenethyst Fragment Felcular 3 % , Ilifar 3 % , Kirith the Damned 3 % , Servant of Sevine 3 % and 4 more","desc":"Well, after that display of voracious greed, I feel nauseous.\nRegardless, I shall not dwell too long on your material addiction.\nFor each imperfect draenethyst fragment you turn in, I shall reward you with more junk. My junk heap gets smaller while your junk heap gets larger. On Draenor we call this a 'win-win' situation.","rew":"You will receive:\nKum'isha's Junk","back":"Well? Draenethyst? Remember?\n<Kum'isha clenches his fist and knocks on your head.>\nIs anybody home?","done":"You truly disgust me, ‹race›. A grown woman drooling over a pile of junk? Pitiful! Take your reward and get out of my sight.\nSounds familiar? It should, because I say it a thousand times per day.\nOh how I loathe this world.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":52,"y":35.6,"n":"Kum'isha the Collector","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2702":{"id":2702,"t":"Heroes of Old","lv":57,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Corporal Thund Splithoof.","desc":"You have honored me with your nobility and heroism, ‹name›.\nYou have also honored them...","rew":"Experience: 3,000","done":"Indeed, you have honored us all. Our thanks alone are not sufficient.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"3822":{"id":3822,"t":"Krom'Grul","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover Sha'ni's Nose-Ring from Krom'Grul and return it to Thal'trak in Kargath. Search the various caves and mines in Dreadmaul Rock.\nSha'ni's Nose-Ring Krom'Grul","desc":"My whole platoon was captured, ‹name›. All were slain - except me.\nTheir leader, Krom'Grul, wanted to save me for some sort of ritual.\nI was chained to this altar and brutalized by the beast. My physical being ceased functioning after an hour of this torture. The beast then ripped my wedding nose-ring off of my face and stuck it on his finger. I had never seen such savagery!\nFind Krom'Grul and kill him! Take my ring back to Thal'trak.\nAnd ‹name›, tell him that we will meet again... in another life.","rew":"You will receive:\nSha'ni's Ring\nExperience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did you find Sha'ni? Is she ok?","done":"<Thal'trak collapses.>\nWe were going to move to the Hinterlands. Did she tell you? This was going to be her last mission.\n<Thal'trak sobs.>\nI don't want it, ‹name›. Keep it, throw it away, I don't care! The ring means nothing to me now. Not without her...\nBadlands Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3.4,"y":48.1,"n":"Thal'trak Proudtusk","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97902":{"id":97902,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Mukdrak in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Mukdrak","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"862":{"id":862,"t":"Dig Rat Stew","lv":23,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Dig Rats to Grub east of the Crossroads.\n8 Dig Rat Dig Rat 0 %","desc":"A ‹class› like you must get pretty hungry out here in The Barrens. Me, I'm starving all day long.\nTell you what, I'll fix you up a nice stew. Just need a few dig rats.\nSeems those filthy dwarves at Bael Modan are overrun with everyone's favorite feast. Now head on down south to Bael Modan and bring me back some dig rats.\nYou can't call yourself a seasoned adventurer until you've spent some time killing rats! Haw!","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Dig Rat Stew 5 Dig Rat Stew Apothecary Gloves\nExperience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Whack enough dig rats yet, ‹name›?","done":"Normally I don't like to eat these rodents when they're so.... so... ripe. Like to let them rot for a few weeks to really bring out the flavor. But you look so hungry.\nLet me fix you some Dig Rat Stew. Ah, there we go.\nHere you go!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":55.3,"y":31.8,"n":"Grub","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94222":{"id":94222,"t":"Craftsmans writ iridescent hammer","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Iridescent Hammer\nIridescent Hammer","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Iridescent Hammer, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Iridescent Hammer Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94222","cats":["crafting"]},"94302":{"id":94302,"t":"Craftsmans writ turtle scale breastplate","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Turtle Scale Breastplate\nTurtle Scale Breastplate","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Turtle Scale Breastplate, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Turtle Scale Breastplate Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94302","cats":["crafting"]},"8222":{"id":8222,"t":"Glowing Scorpid Blood","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Glowing Scorpid Blood Firetail Scorpid 30.3 % , Stonelash Pincer 29.4 % , Stonelash Flayer 28.2 % , Deathlash Scorpid 21.2 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"In all my time working the Faire, I've learned a lot of things about customers. Here's one of those nuggets of wisdom: customers love stuff that glows! It doesn't matter what it is - you could take a broken chair leg and make it glow, and every child will come from miles around to get one!\nSo, ‹name›, I need glowing scorpid blood. You can find it from the scorpids of Sillithus, or the Blasted Lands, or the Burning Steppes.","done":"Great job, ‹name›! Thanks a lot! I'm going to make paint from this blood and turn all kinds of cheap junk into glowing treasure!\nHere are your tickets, and thanks again!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7902":{"id":7902,"t":"Vibrant Plumes","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Vibrant Plume Snowblind Harpy 35.8 % in Alterac Valley , Snowblind Ambusher 35.1 % in Alterac Valley , Sky Shadow 33.6 % , Carrion Vulture 30.1 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n12 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"A person's imagination is an incredible thing. It can make the smallest hill seem like the largest mountain. It can make the most innocuous shadow appear cast by a horrible nightmare!\nWe at the Darkmoon Faire let our visitor's imaginations blossom! But to help stretch their imaginations... sometimes we have to get tricky.\nI need vibrant plumes for one of my attractions. You can get them from the birds of the more dangerous areas of Azeroth. Bring me the plumes and many tickets will be yours!","done":"Ah, the plumes! They are amazing, don't you think! It would be easy to spark one's imaginations with such beauties!\nYou do such charitable work, ‹name›. The smiles on our visitors' faces when they see the show is a grand payment indeed, but please take these tickets as well.\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"942":{"id":942,"t":"The Absent Minded Prospector","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the mysterious fossil to Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor.\nMysterious Fossil\nProvided: Mysterious Fossil","desc":"This fossil bears a striking resemblance to one I once saw in Ironforge. An archaeologist by the name of Flagongut brought it to our annual Explorers' League conference. He believed the fossil had a power which could be unlocked somehow.\nLast I heard Flagongut had holed up in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, awaiting escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site. Seek him out and show him Remtravel's fossil. Perhaps he can reveal the secrets of the past.\nThe ship to Menethil departs from Auberdine.","rew":"Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"What ya got there, friend?","done":"Oh my! You say this came from the distant lands of Kalimdor?\nAmazing! Simply amazing!\nDarnassus Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.2,"y":84.5,"n":"Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.8,"y":60.4,"n":"Archaeologist Flagongut","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6142":{"id":6142,"t":"Clam Bait","lv":35,"min":31,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find 10 pieces of Soft-shelled Clam Meat and bring it back to Mai'Lahii at Shadowprey Village.\n10 Soft-shelled Clam Meat Drysnap Pincer , Drysnap Crawler , Slitherblade Oracle , Slitherblade Myrmidon and 4 more","desc":"You have the look of a fisherman, ‹class›! I love to fish - been fishing all my life. The best bait to use is soft-shelled clam meat; the fish just can't resist, you know what I mean?\nUp north you will find a wrecked ship off the coast. Soft-shelled clams are littered throughout the area. If you bring me back 10 pieces of soft-shelled clam meat, I will give you something in return.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPardoc Grips Ringtail Girdle Bracesteel Belt\nExperience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I can't wait to go fishing with some fresh soft-shelled clam meat; did you bring me the 10 pieces of it I need?","done":"Perfect mon, this is just what the witch doctor told me to do for my headache. He says, \"\"Mai'Lahii - go fish. It'll make you feel better\"\"\nWell, I feel better already, thanks mon!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":22.6,"y":72,"n":"Mai'Lahii","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"96222":{"id":96222,"t":"Khan hratha","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Maraudine Key Fragment to Umarak in the Desolace.\nMaraudine Key Fragment\nWar Horn Mouthpiece","desc":"While war rages throughout the region, the Maraudine centaur stand unchallenged in the Valley of Spears. I worry that they will grow callous in time and stir further unrest if the other clans continue to turn a blind eye to their presence.\nKhan Hratha possesses a Maraudine Key Fragment, and I wish to have it as a negotiation tactic. Find a war horn mouthpiece from the centaur there and use it to challenge him atop the highest peak.\nBring the key to me, and I will have a proposition for you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKolkar Marauder Chain Traitor's Finger Kolkar Hunter's Belt Ceremonial Centaur Blanket\nYou will also receive:\n10 Carved Centaur Totem\nMoney: 1 15 1 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,300","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":43.4,"y":78.8,"n":"Umarak","s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7502":{"id":7502,"t":"Harnessing Shadows","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nHarnessing Shadows A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: Harnessing Shadows","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: Harnessing Shadows End Lorekeeper Mykos Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Warlock Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7502","cats":["dire-maul"]},"222":{"id":222,"t":"Worgen in the Woods","lv":31,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Nightbane Vile Fang and 8 Nightbane Tainted One worgen for Calor in Darkshire.\nNightbane Vile Fang slain : 0/ 8\nNightbane Tainted One slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Your previous accomplishments have convinced me that you are ready to take on the toughest worgen infesting the woods.\nOf the worgen that have made their new home here, the Vile Fangs and the Tainted Ones have proven the most dangerous. They've settled down near some of the caves and in the mine to the south.\nFrom far away you can even see the light from their bonfires...","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,900\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Intimidating beasts aren't they? But have no fear, ‹name›, those who stand for the Light will never fall!","done":"‹name›, to be honest with you, I did not believe that you would get this far, but you are clearly a ‹class› to be reckoned with. In fact, if you wish to formally join Master Carevin's struggle, I will gladly write for you a letter of recommendation.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Calor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1262":{"id":1262,"t":"Report to Zor","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Jeweled Pendant to Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar.\nJeweled Pendant Muckshell Razorclaw 5 % , Muckshell Scrabbler 5 % , Muckshell Pincer 5 % , Muckshell Snapclaw 5 % and 2 more\nProvided: Jeweled Pendant","desc":"It is strange that the pendant Marg stole was in the hands of common soldiers. Perhaps its owner was in disguise, or perhaps the soldiers themselves stole it!\nRegardless of which is true, this is a noble's pendant and we must discover its true owner if we are to unravel its mystery.\nTake the pendant to Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar. He is well schooled in Alliance politics, and will know if this pendant has a history among the nobles of Stormwind.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You traveled from Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow? How fares Nazeer, and how fare his efforts in the marsh?","done":"This pendant was crafted with great skill and precision, ‹name›. No orc would covet such a jewel...\nBut many humans would.\nI will have this pendant studied. In time let us hope that its mysteries will be revealed to us.\nDustwallow Marsh Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Zor Lonetree","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5742":{"id":5742,"t":"Redemption","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen to what Tirion Fordring has to say.","desc":"You have worked hard, friend. Rest your weary bones and allow me to properly introduce myself.","rew":"Experience: 575","back":"Please, friend; sit and hear my tale.","done":"The Fordring redemption will be a difficult task. Are you prepared?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9182":{"id":9182,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Huge Thorium Battleaxe","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 3 Huge Thorium Battleaxes and the Craftsman's Writ - Huge Thorium Battleaxe - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Huge Thorium Battleaxe\n3 Huge Thorium Battleaxe\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Huge Thorium Battleaxe","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order BS-6020:\n3 Huge Thorium Battleaxes.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"These aren't as huge as I expected. Regardless, a deal is a deal.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"62":{"id":62,"t":"The Fargodeep Mine","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Explore the Fargodeep Mine, then return to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"The mine in Northshire isn't the only one with problems! I have reports that the Fargodeep Mine in Elwynn has also become a haven for Kobolds.\nExplore the mine and confirm these reports, then return to me. The mine is almost due south of Goldshire, between the Stonefield and Maclure homesteads.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 480\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What do you have to report, ‹name›? Have you been to the Fargodeep Mine?","done":"This is bad news. What's next, dragons?!? We'll have to increase our patrols near that mine. Thanks for your efforts, ‹name›. And hold a moment... I might have another task for you.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4462":{"id":4462,"t":"Corrupted Night Dragon","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a Night Dragon plant. The fruits that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 4 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Night Dragon. It immediately begins to shed it's corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":35.1,"y":58.9,"n":"Corrupted Night Dragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4222":{"id":4222,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.3,"y":48.7,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8462":{"id":8462,"t":"Speak to Nafien","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel north along the main road in Felwood and speak with the furbolg named Nafien. He stands guard outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold.","desc":"Perhaps you are capable of handling a larger threat that we Timbermaw face. You certainly have shown yourself capable here...\nAnother of my kind stands guard outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold, along this road far to the north. His name is Nafien; while he may appear to be a feral and unsavory beast, fear him not. He only seeks aid against the malign forces that threaten our home.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","done":"Ah... I have heard the word on the wind about those not of our tribe who seek to ally themselves with the Timbermaw furbolgs. I welcome you, but you must be warned that my tribe reacts poorly to strangers.\nThese are trying times, and we can only trust those who choose to fight the corruption of the land alongside of us... and have proven themselves to us accordingly. Those who have not done so will be met with open hostility should they enter the Hold.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.9,"y":85,"n":"Grazle","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":64.8,"y":8.1,"n":"Nafien","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2862":{"id":2862,"t":"War on the Woodpaw","lv":42,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Woodpaw Gnoll Manes to Hadoken Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n10 Woodpaw Gnoll Mane Woodpaw Alpha 60 % , Woodpaw Reaver 60 % , Woodpaw Mystic 60 % , Woodpaw Brute 60 % and 2 more","desc":"The gnolls... they are more than a nuisance. They are a constant threat to the existence of this very camp! It is irrelevant whether they are indigenous to Feralas or not; if we do not strengthen our resolve against them, we will find ourselves driven out of the entire region.\nThe gnoll attacks against the camp have become more fevered as of late. We need your aid in thinning their numbers; bring to me ten of their manes, and I will reward you handsomely for your effort.\nGo!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"We drive them back, and yet they still attack! Someone or something must be driving them into a frenzy... oh, you have returned, eh ‹name›? Do you have the manes I require for the bounty to be met?","done":"This is proof of a good start, ‹name›. Your skills as a soldier are to be commended.\nYou are not the only one I ask that task of. Many before you have fought them, and in times past our efforts have kept them at bay. Recently though, their attempts to push northward into our area of influence have increased dramatically. Their attacks have also become more savage... almost as if they were desperate.\nI have a plan though, ‹name›, that might settle things once and for all against them...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2942":{"id":2942,"t":"The Morrow Stone","lv":50,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Sparkling Stone and the Stave of Equinex to Troyas Moonbreeze in Feathermoon Stronghold.\nA Sparkling Stone\nStave of Equinex\nProvided: Stave of Equinex","desc":"The moment the artifact is removed from the Monolith, you feel the energy in the Stave of Equinex begin to fade.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCairnstone Sliver Seedtime Hoop\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I am glad you have returned, ‹name›. I am eager to hear of your findings.","done":"I have been reading since you left, ‹name›. This stone you have found is called the Morrow Stone. While I am not entirely sure what its purpose is yet, you can be sure that it is something of great significance to be hidden away inside the Equinex Monolith the way it was.\nI will continue my studies, and I hope I will be able to count on you in the future, ‹name›. Thank you for all your help.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":38.8,"y":13.2,"n":"Equinex Monolith","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":31.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Troyas Moonbreeze","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6622":{"id":6622,"t":"Triage","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries.\nRemember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.\nProvided: Triage Bandage","desc":"Good day, doctor. You will be tested on your ability to triage patients accordingly this afternoon. Should you pass your examination, you will join the prestigious ranks of Horde Trauma.\nNow pay attention! The critically injured must be tended to first. After the criticals come the badly injured. The injured should be tended to last. You must save 15 patients to pass this exam. You will fail should 6 of your patients die in triage.\nTriage bandages will be supplied.\nGood luck, doctor.","rew":"You will learn: First Aid\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Miraculous work, doctor. Simply miraculous.","done":"Doctor ‹name›, welcome to Horde Trauma.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.4,"y":36.9,"n":"Doctor Gregory Victor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["first-aid"]},"6062":{"id":6062,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Dire Mottled Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Thotar in Razor Hill.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"It is an admirable skill to command one's authority over nature. As a hunter, you must strive to learn to use the force and power inherent to any creature of your choosing.\nGaining control of an animal is not an easy feat; it is a task that you must undertake with much determination.\nFor your first assignment, take this taming rod and use it to tame a dire mottled boar. You can find them quite close to Razor Hill. Practice your skills in battle with the boar at your side, then return to me.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Good luck, young ‹class›.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. I believe you are ready for your next task.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9262":{"id":9262,"t":"Investigate the Scourge of Darnassus","lv":10,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 625 experience instead of 650, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Darnassus and investigate the glowing runic circles near their encampment.\n3 Dim Necrotic Stone Skeletal Soldier 35 % , Spectral Apparition 35 % , Spectral Spirit 31 % , Skeletal Trooper 31 %","desc":"The Lich King has sent his undead upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Darnassus from these accursed invaders?\nThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you. Go!","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625","back":"Have you investigated the invasion yet? There's no time for dawdling!","done":"Hmm. From what you've told me, the voices within the circles... they must be used for communication of some kind. I shudder to think what unnatural minds are contacted through such magic. Regardless, you seem to have emerged whole and sane. The Argent Dawn appreciates your service.\nDarnassus Elwynn Forest Tirisfal Glades Dun Morogh Mulgore Durotar Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":77.9,"y":42.4,"n":"Lieutenant Beitha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"7342":{"id":7342,"t":"Arrows Are For Sissies","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"200 Thorium Shells sold by Jimmy McWeaksauce","rew":"You will receive:\n200 Thorium Headed Arrow","back":"Can you believe this rubbish?! The last shipment of ammunition from Kharanos was botched! All we have for ammo now are these flimsy, good for nothing arrows! What in the world am I going to do with 500,000 thorium headed arrows?\nI'll tell you what, kid. If you can bring me thorium shells, I'll trade you thorium headed arrows - straight up! Deal?","done":"A done deal if I ever saw one! The arrows are yours.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.2,"y":29.4,"n":"Artilleryman Sheldonore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"1582":{"id":1582,"t":"Moonglow Vest","lv":18,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Embossed Leather Gloves, 5 Embossed Leather Boots and 5 Embossed Leather Cloaks to Lotherias in Darnassus.\nEmbossed Leather Gloves\n5 Embossed Leather Boots\n5 Embossed Leather Cloak","desc":"We in Darnassus, especially we craftsman, are quite busy. Young adventurers are eager to test themselves in the wilderness, and are in constant need of supplies.\nIf you can help me fill my orders of leather goods, then perhaps I can teach you an advanced leatherworking technique.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Moonglow Vest\nExperience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings, ‹name›.","done":"Yes, these are good pieces. You have a skilled hand and an eye for detail. Your future as a leatherworker is promising.\nHere, ‹name›. Let me show you the pattern to make the Moonglow Vest.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":64.4,"y":22.2,"n":"Lotherias","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"302":{"id":302,"t":"Powder to Ironband","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.","desc":"If Ironband still needs blastpowder, then by Magni he'll have it! I sent the approval on ahead with a messenger to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar. He'll prepare the powder and other supplies to take to Ironband.\nAnd one more thing: I want you to personally see that the shipment of powder reaches its destination. The last one didn't, so keep your mind sharp and your eyes open.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"What? Stormpike wants you to personally see the shipment to Ironband?\nI... suppose that's fine, the only problem is, I've already sent Huldar with the porters, Miran and Saean. You just missed them, they left just a short while ago.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.2,"y":47.4,"n":"Jern Hornhelm","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"3182":{"id":3182,"t":"Proof of Deed","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 1g 40s instead of 1g 20s.","obj":"Take Margol's Gigantic Horn to Curator Thorius in Ironforge.\nMargol's Gigantic Horn\nProvided: Margol's Gigantic Horn","desc":"You expect me to believe a story like that? The real horn would have had my broken axe head still lodged into its surface.\nListen, take that obvious fake to Curator Thorius in Ironforge. If he can validate your claim, you will receive a proof of deed. Bring that proof back to me and I'll give you the key to the Searing Gorge.\nGet going!","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Why hello there young lady. Would you like a tour of the museum?","done":"What's this?\nOh my, I don't believe it! Do you realize what you've got here, ‹race›? This is the horn of Margol the Rager! Margol, the bane of every archaeologist that ever set foot in the Searing Gorge.\nMay I keep it?\nLoch Modan Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":18.2,"y":84,"n":"Mountaineer Pebblebitty","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Curator Thorius","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8862":{"id":8862,"t":"Elune's Candle","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nElune's Candle Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"Elune's candle is an artifact of great reverence to the disciples of the Lunar Festival. Stored within the candle is true moonlight, ready to be unleashed!\nThis light is harmless to most creatures, but you will find that Omen and his minions are burned and dazzled by it.","done":"Very well then - I accept these coins of ancestry. Please take Elune's candle with my blessing. Also, please enjoy these complimentary fireworks.\nMay your Lunar Festival be joyous and filled with merriment, ‹name›.\nAnd if you choose to face Omen and his minions, you will find Elune's candle quite useful...","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Valadar Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9102":{"id":9102,"t":"Frostfire Bindings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Frostfire Bindings if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Bindings, 6 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 1 Arcane Crystal and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Bindings Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\nNexus Crystal","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Bindings\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Bindings.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9022":{"id":9022,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Boots of Valor, Legplates of Valor and Spaulders of Valor.\nBoots of Valor Kirtonos the Herald 0 %\nLegplates of Valor Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nSpaulders of Valor Warchief Rend Blackhand 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nBoots of Heroism Legplates of Heroism Spaulders of Heroism\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8942":{"id":8942,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Cord of Elements and a set of Gauntlets of Elements to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nCord of Elements Smolderthorn Witch Doctor 4.4 % , Rage Talon Flamescale 3.8 % , Bloodaxe Evoker 2.5 % , Firebrand Pyromancer 2.4 % and 3 more\nGauntlets of Elements Pyroguard Emberseer 0 %","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gauntlets. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nCord of The Five Thunders Gauntlets of The Five Thunders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5662":{"id":5662,"t":"Touch of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"My respect to you and your kind, ‹name›. I normally teach only those of my own tribe. Your lessons come from Aelthalyste in the city once called Lordaeron.\nYou should return to her if you're to learn those abilities that set you apart from other faiths.\nGo to the War Quarter in the Undercity and find your mistress there.","rew":"You will learn: Touch of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"Ah, good, another has arrived. Time may not matter to me, but to you it is of the essence. There is much for you to learn and there is much I wish to teach you. You simply must prove your worth. Do that, and you shall be greatly rewarded.\nOrgrimmar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"1102":{"id":1102,"t":"A Vengeful Fate","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,500 experience instead of 4,050, 2.1 times as much. New rewards: Quilboar Blaster. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring Razorflank's Heart to Auld Stonespire in Thunder Bluff.\nRazorflank's Heart Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul","desc":"Cairne is a noble leader for uniting our people here on Thunder Bluff.\nBut I cannot forgive those who drove us from our ancestral lands as easily as some. My people inhabited the southern Barrens for decades. The land was holy to us. But we were driven off by numerous foes.\nA vengeful fate awaits the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who musters a foul army from within Razorfen Kraul.\nBring me Razorflank's heart and I can die in peace, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBerylline Pads Stonefist Girdle Marbled Buckler\nNew in Forever: Quilboar Blaster.\nYou will also receive:\nQuilboar Blaster\nExperience: 8,500\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Once I know the foul beasts of Razorfen Kraul have been driven from their foul lair, I will be able to rest in peace, knowing that revenge has been served.\nHave you the driven the quilboar from the Kraul? Do you bring to me good news in the form of Razorflank's heart?","done":"I see the nasty tribe of Razorfen Kraul now knows the pain of my people. Serves the foul beasts right.\nTo drive one from a holy land is a sin worthy of the most severe revenge.\nThank you, ‹name›, for aiding me in my plight.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":36,"y":59.9,"n":"Auld Stonespire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-kraul"]},"3102":{"id":3102,"t":"Encrypted Letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Letter and speak to Jorik Kerridan in the stable behind Northshire Abbey.\nEncrypted Letter\nProvided: Encrypted Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Jorik, one of our local trainers. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You made it here in one piece, and it doesn't look like too many people saw you. Good enough for me. I don't like to have much attention drawn to me back here... nice and quiet. I'm sure you can understand.\nHave any trouble yet? I'm glad to hear not. That'll change soon enough.","done":"You're gonna find that there a number of outfits that'll covet our skills, ‹name›. Adventurers, SI:7... heck, even the Defias Brotherhood wouldn't mind a spy or two inside Stormwind. But you remember this, you're your own man. Don't let nobody bully you into doing something you don't wanna do! Besides, we hold all the cards... at least, we do before the game's done. Know what I mean?\nAnyway, just wanted to introduce myself and let you know that I'm here if you need any training. Come by anytime.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":50.3,"y":39.9,"n":"Jorik Kerridan","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2382":{"id":2382,"t":"Wrenix of Ratchet","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Ratchet and speak with Wrenix the Wretched.","desc":"Zando'zan has seen it! Yes, the day comes! Thrall's death... the dagger in his back, poison seeping through to his every vein... Zando'zan has said too much.\n‹name›! Zando'zan has a task for ‹name›! ‹name› must travel to Ratchet, east of the Crossroads, and speak with Wrenix the Wretched. Go!","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"Another one? The last five that crazy troll sent me ended up as shark food. Let's hope you fare a little better, eh?\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.7,"y":53,"n":"Zando'zan","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.1,"y":36.3,"n":"Wrenix the Wretched","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"96782":{"id":96782,"t":"Covert extraction","lv":36,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Blade of House Perenolde and the Royal Aegis of Perenolde among the ruins of Alterac. Then, bring them to Myrokos Silentform.\nBlade of House Perenolde\nRoyal Aegis of Perenolde","desc":"It seems our friend Barton here has made this very easy for us. He is after two heirlooms of the Perenolde family within the ruins of Alterac. The Blade of House Perenolde, a sword, and the Royal Aegis of Perenolde, a shield.\nFrom the report, it seems these armaments are within two towers among the ruins. Best we acquire them before the Syndicate does.\nThe ogres occupying the ruins are fierce, but I trust you should be able to sneak past them without needing to bloody your blade at all.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Ravenholdt\nLevel 36 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 32 34 39 46 Side Both factions Class Rogue Shareable Yes Quest ID 96782\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 36, 5,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 36 ] What's the Big Idea?\nSteal Barton's Scouting Report by pickpocketing it from him.\nMyrokos Silentform Alterac Mountains\n2,800 XP\n2 [ 36 ] Covert Extraction this quest\nFind the Blade of House Perenolde and the Royal Aegis of Perenolde among the ruins of Alterac.\n2,800 XP","cats":["rogue"]},"5582":{"id":5582,"t":"Healthy Dragon Scale","lv":58,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Healthy Dragon Scale to Betina Bigglezink at the Light's Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands.\nHealthy Dragon Scale Plagued Hatchling 6 % in Scholomance\nProvided: Healthy Dragon Scale","desc":"This is a scale shed from a plagued dragon hatchling. But unlike the other pocked, oozing scales on the infant beast, this rare scale is healthy and unmarred.\nBetina Bigglezink will want a sample of this to study.","back":"‹name›, do you have something to show me?","done":"Excellent! This will be invaluable in my continued studies of the machinations of the Scourge. Thank you, ‹name›, and if you find more of these scales please bring them to me!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Betina Bigglezink","e":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"7022":{"id":7022,"t":"Greatfather Winter is Here!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Ironforge.","desc":"Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend! Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter! If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil. Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!\nAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year. We have a great selection to choose from. Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.\nIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.\nUndercity Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":68.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Nardstrum Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8382":{"id":8382,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Leggings Sandstorm Boots\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"9422":{"id":9422,"t":"Scouring the Desert","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 55.","obj":"Find and deliver Silithyst to the Silithyst Extractor then speak with General Kirika at the Horde encampment near Hive'Regal.\nDeliver Silithyst","desc":"For some time now, we have been tapping the crystal resources of the Silithus desert. The only dangers we faced were from the creatures that made this place their home and the oppressive sand and dust and heat.\nBut now the Alliance seems to have caught on to what we have found here. It is now a race between us to capture the natural resources, and keep them from the other.\nI need every set of hands that is available. I hope I have yours.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n2 Major Healing Potion 2 Major Mana Potion\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Be wary of the dangers of the desert, ‹name›. With the Alliance lurking in the dunes, any step could be your last.","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. These resources will be added to our stockpiles, and every bit is to our gain and our enemy's loss.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":69.5,"n":"General Kirika","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8302":{"id":8302,"t":"The Hand of the Righteous","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 200 Silithid Carapace Fragments and return to Baristolth.\n200 Silithid Carapace Fragment Supreme Silithid Flayer , Hive'Regal Hive Lord , Hive'Regal Slavemaker , Hive'Regal Spitfire and 4 more","desc":"Choose your deputies wisely, mortal. Each time you return with your task complete, a new deputy you will be allowed to choose.\nWith that said, I require more of the carapace fragments. Waste no time!","rew":"You will receive:\nProxy of Nozdormu\nExperience: 650\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Perhaps one day the whole of Cenarion Hold will be working under your command.","done":"Well done, hero. You will now be granted the ability to deputize another Agent of Nozdormu.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":36.4,"n":"Baristolth of the Shifting Sands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8782":{"id":8782,"t":"Uniform Supplies","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Mooncloth, 2 Bolts of Runecloth and 1 Ironweb Spider Silk to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.\nMooncloth\n2 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\nIronweb Spider Silk Mother Smolderweb 50 % , Crystal Fang 47 % , Gretheer 16.2 % , Plague Lurker 13.9 % and 4 more\nLogistics Task Briefing VIII\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing VIII","desc":"The latest influx of volunteers has caused a shortage of uniforms. Procure a batch of uniform materials and bring them to Windcaller Proudhorn.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78142":{"id":78142,"t":"Bewitchments and glamours","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bewitchments and Glamours","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nBewitchments and Glamours (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"5502":{"id":5502,"t":"A Warden of the Horde","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return your ward to the Orgrimmar orphanage by handing in the Orcish Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Battlewail in the Valley of Honor.\nOrcish Orphan Whistle","desc":"You have been so very kind to me, ‹name›. I never dreamed that I'd have so much fun during Children's Week. Thank you. I won't be sad about what's happened to me - my parents always told me to rise above anything bad that happens. I'll be a hero... just like you.\nI'm sad to say this, but it's time for me to go home. Let's go back and I'll tell the matron what an awesome person you are!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPiglet's Collar Rat Cage Turtle Box Curmudgeon's Payoff\nExperience: 1,650\n+200 reputation with Horde","back":"It is a pleasure to see you again, ‹name›. Have you attended to the duties you've volunteered for during Children's Week?","done":"May the spirits bless you, ‹name›. You've done more for Grunth than most would ever think of doing for him. Thank you - you're the epitome of what it means to be a hero of the Horde.\nPlease - if you can spare the time, come back and visit us. I know that Grunth would like that, as would I.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":70.7,"y":25.2,"n":"Orphan Matron Battlewail","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"6542":{"id":6542,"t":"Report to Kadrak","lv":19,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.","desc":"Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.\nIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders.","rew":"Experience: 150","done":"Ashenvale is a divided land, but our most recent efforts have been very successful. We not only have an outpost at the Zoram Strand, but another just north of here called Splintertree.\nStonetalon Mountains The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":73.2,"y":94.9,"n":"Darn Talongrip","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.1,"y":5.4,"n":"Kadrak","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"542":{"id":542,"t":"Return to Milton","lv":38,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tomes of Alterac to Milton Sheaf in Stormwind.\nTomes of Alterac\nProvided: Tomes of Alterac","desc":"I need to spend some time studying the Arm of Gri'lek book you brought me, though I'm sure Milton is eager to get the other recovered books into Stormwind's collection.\nHere are the books you gathered from the Ruins of Alterac, packed and catalogued. Take them back to Milton Sheaf in Stormwind and I'm sure he'll be grateful.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, you've returned! How did your foray into Alterac go? Did you bring anything back with you?","done":"My oh my! Look at these! I can't believe they survived the ruination of Alterac. And all those ogres too!\nThank you, ‹name›. Thank you so much! You have helped preserve human knowledge, and you add to the grandeur of the Royal Library of Stormwind.\nHillsbrad Foothills Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":30.2,"n":"Milton Sheaf","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"622":{"id":622,"t":"Return to Corporal Kaleb","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Krazek's Fixed Pot to Corporal Kaleb at the Rebel Camp.\nKrazek's Fixed Pot\nProvided: Krazek's Fixed Pot","desc":"While you were gone I fixed the pot you brought me. I even added an extra steam whistle, and look! There's a new chopper at the bottom that'll cut through leg bones!\nYes yes, Krazek's Crock Pot is a 100% cook pleaser! I'm sure its owner will be satisfied.","rew":"You will receive:\nCap of Harmony\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Did you make it to Booty Bay? Did the goblin Krazek fix my pot??","done":"It's fixed! This is great, now I can get dinner started! Thanks so much, ‹name›.\nI hope you were okay in Booty Bay. That place can get pretty rough, and... I heard rumors that the goblins will sometimes drag drunk sailors to their slave boats and take them to who-knows-where... to do who-knows-what...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.7,"y":3.3,"n":"Corporal Kaleb","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8062":{"id":8062,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Predator's Bracers","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring the following Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub to Falthir the Sightless: A Primal Hakkari Bindings. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Bindings\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"In the dark times after the fall of the Gurubashi Empire, Zandalar predators used their prowess to provide sustenance for the tribe. Hunters claim to be much like our tribe's predators - to seek the hunt is to embody the essence of the predator, yes. Your hunt in Zul'Gurub, however, will show us how you truly rate amongst our finest predators.\nBring to me a sampling of the Paragons of Power from within Zul'Gurub. Do so, and you'll take first steps in becoming the penultimate predator.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Predator's Bracers\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Hunt those in Zul'Gurub that would possess the Paragons of Power, ‹name›. They are your prey; they possess that which we both must have.","done":"Yes... I need no vision to sense the presence of the Paragons of Power. Your success in Zul'Gurub has impressed many among the tribe. We not only consider you to be a friend of the Zandalar, but also consider you worthy enough to possess the predator's bracers - powerful items, and a symbol of what it means to be a predator. Well done, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5262":{"id":5262,"t":"The Truth Comes Crashing Down","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Head of Balnazzar to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nHead of Balnazzar Balnazzar\nProvided: Head of Balnazzar","desc":"You try and gather your thoughts as the dust settles across the chamber. You go over the events that just transpired and still cannot comprehend the gravity of the situation.\nThe Grand Crusader of the Scarlet Crusade a demon? And not just any demon but brother to Varimathras, arch lord of the Undercity?\nYou carefully stow the severed head of the dreadlord into your pack. Surely, none would believe the tale you would tell without proof.\nDuke Nicholas Zverenhoff must be told at once!","rew":"Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"What have you got there, ‹name›?","done":"What will this mean to the Crusade? Could it be possible that they have been under the control of this demon? Unwittingly serving as the pawns to a greater evil?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"1422":{"id":1422,"t":"Threat From the Sea","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.","desc":"While I begin work on your weapon, why don't you talk to Katar? He mentioned needing help with patrols along the beach, and I'd rather see you keep your wits and weapons prepared instead of getting drunk with some of the other louses I share this camp with.","done":"Be silent a moment, ‹class›. Even over the dull roar of the sea you can still hear those disgusting gurgles from the fish men.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":81.3,"y":81,"n":"Tok'Kar","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":83.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Katar","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"2622":{"id":2622,"t":"The Missing Orders","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Bengor.","desc":"The orders? What could you possibly want with the orders?\nWhat are you implying, ‹name›? Of course I relayed those orders! The soldiers I sent the orders with were ambushed and brutally beaten by murlocs. Only one survived, if you can call that surviving. He can hardly speak, cannot walk, and must be fed through a tube. If you want to know what happened to those orders, speak with Bengor. I'm sure he is around here somewhere... and, ‹name›, be mindful of what you stick your nose into - it may get bitten off.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","done":"Swamp tal... talk.. talker...","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.8,"y":54.9,"n":"Dispatch Commander Ruag","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":45,"y":57.4,"n":"Bengor","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"3022":{"id":3022,"t":"Handle With Care","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Carefully-packed Crate to Erelas Ambersky in Rut'theran Village.\nA Carefully-packed Crate\nProvided: A Carefully-packed Crate","desc":"‹name›, I can see you yearn to be dedicated to my worthwhile cause. Yes, of course, you can do something for me!\nTake this crate of eggs to Erelas Ambersky. He is a druid that cares for these eggs, helping them to hatch and then training the young hippogryphs. You will find him in Teldrassil, in a small village to the south called Rut'theran.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100","back":"Another shipment from Curgle, I assume?","done":"Thank you for your help, ‹name›. The hippogryph population simply wouldn't flourish if it weren't for us. Ah, but I am sure you understand all too well, having traveled to Feralas yourself, and seen the devastation of the Gordunni there.\nWell, as you can see, I am hard at work here, so you'd best be on your way.\nThanks again, ‹name›.\nTanaris Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.5,"y":92,"n":"Erelas Ambersky","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"6382":{"id":6382,"t":"The Ashenvale Hunt","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.","desc":"Your strength impresses me, ‹class›. Your willingness to embrace the hunt gives me confidence that you could move on to bigger game... and bigger challenges.\nThe forests of Ashenvale represent a vast untamed wild that the Horde seeks to impose its own will upon, both politically and spiritually. If you seek to prove yourself in an unproven land, seek the guidance of Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post. The outpost is due north of the path leading from the Barrens.","rew":"Experience: 390\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Welcome to the new frontier, ‹name›. Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young ‹class› like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle. Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.\nYour presence here tells me that you've come to learn more about the hunt. Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.\nThe Barrens Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2782":{"id":2782,"t":"Rin'ji's Secret","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Oran Snakewrithe, a well known scholar on matters concerning the Witherbark trolls, may be able to decipher the tablet. She is known to reside within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\nRin'ji's Secret\nProvided: Rin'ji's Secret","desc":"The tablet is covered with Witherbark troll markings. Rin'ji's secret truly is a mystery...\nIt's possible that you might have something quite valuable on your hands here. On the other hand, quite the opposite is also possible. A Witherbark troll in distress would probably do anything to find his way out of trouble...","rew":"Experience: 2,100\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Well, now, what is this?","done":"This tablet... Quite unusual... Where did you find this, ‹name›?\nThe Hinterlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":86.3,"y":59,"n":"Rin'ji's Secret","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.1,"y":32.8,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"4542":{"id":4542,"t":"Message to Freewind Post","lv":25,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Urgent Message to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post.\nUrgent Message\nProvided: Urgent Message","desc":"Brave traveler, the centaurs have increased their attacks in this area. Freewind Post must know about this renewed harassment immediately! Seek Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post to the southeast and give him this urgent message.\nBe warned, avoid the Grimtotem Clan nearby... they have been acting strange toward us lately.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 500\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"What do you want, ‹class›? An urgent message - for me?","done":"More bad news! These centaurs have gone too far! They raided one of my supply caravans and slaughtered the whole party. This is an outrage, and it will not go unpunished!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":32.2,"y":22.2,"n":"Brave Moonhorn","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":45.7,"y":50.7,"n":"Cliffwatcher Longhorn","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1182":{"id":1182,"t":"Goblin Sponsorship","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Fuel Regulator Blueprints to Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.\nFuel Regulator Blueprints Cozzle's Footlocker","desc":"See, the Venture Company shredders out in Lake Nazferiti (in northern Stranglethorn) have been equipped with a new model fuel regulator. I was thinking that Pozzik would be able to take advantage of it, if he could get some details. Unfortunately, Cozzle, the foreman out there, appears to be a little more clever than I gave him credit for.\nYou seem like you might have more luck finding the blueprints though. I know he keeps them in his house, but they're almost certainly under lock and key.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Much as I hate to admit it, that gnome team they have out there is pretty good. Our boys need every edge they can get.","done":"Now, let me just get a copy of these blueprints for my own notes and you can bring these straight to Pozzik. Wouldn't want him to think that one of his sponsors was abandoning him.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7662":{"id":7662,"t":"New Kodo - Teal","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Teal Kodo","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGreat Brown Kodo Great Gray Kodo Great White Kodo","back":"If you bring me your aging kodo, I will trade it in for one from the new herd. The new kodo will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the great kodos we already have around the yard here to see what you will have to choose from.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.7,"y":62.1,"n":"Harb Clawhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"7822":{"id":7822,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by Thunder Bluff, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":43,"y":42.7,"n":"Rumstag Proudstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"3902":{"id":3902,"t":"Scavenging Deathknell","lv":3,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search Deathknell and the vicinity for 6 pieces of Scavenged Goods, and return them to Deathguard Saltain.\n6 Scavenged Goods Equipment Boxes","desc":"You there! If you're looking for something to make yourself useful, then listen up!\nWe need fresh out-of-the-ground recruits to head into Deathknell and search for any sort of useful equipment. Most likely, they'll be in stacks of boxes. We expect more recruits to be rising soon, and unless we want them to stumble about naked we had better get to scavenging!\nWell get to work, you miserable bag of bones! I'm not going to reward those without some hustle.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlax Belt Rustmetal Bracers Short Duskbat Cape\nExperience: 320\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you managed to scavenge up some useful items for us? There is no shame in reusing that which has been tossed aside. No one is going to give us any handouts - we Forsaken will fend for ourselves!","done":"Great work ‹name›, I knew you weren't useless. Here - have one of the better items I've found out of the lots that have been collected so far.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31.6,"y":65.6,"n":"Deathguard Saltain","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"382":{"id":382,"t":"The Red Messenger","lv":5,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Meven Korgal, the messenger, at the Crusader camp, then return any information you find to Executor Arren.\nScarlet Crusade Documents Meven Korgal","desc":"Reports from my superiors in Brill indicate that an agent of the Scarlet Crusade was dispatched from the Scarlet Monastery and sent here to Deathknell. According to the reports, the messenger possesses important information on his person. I do not have further details, but whatever it is, we must have it!\nYou're the most qualified person I have to send, ‹name›. Find that messenger and bring me whatever information you can find.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nExecutor Staff Deathguard Buckler\nExperience: 675\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"How goes your mission, ‹name›?","done":"Hmm... Let's see what you've got...\n<He begins to rifle through the documents you recovered.>\nSome news of their exploits against us... Worthless. Scouting reports... New orders, \"Continue to build up a camp near the ruined city...\" Nothing we didn't know already... Ah, what's this? A map of the dispositions of some of their field commanders and agents! We can use this.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.2,"y":66,"n":"Executor Arren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"5902":{"id":5902,"t":"A Plague Upon Thee","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find someplace suitable in the center of the Northridge Lumber Mill in Western Plaguelands to place the Barrel of Plagueland Termites.\nProvided: Barrel of Plagueland Termites","desc":"Now that we have plenty of termites, take this steel reinforced barrel to the Northridge Lumber Mill south of Hearthglen--you'll find it to the west of the road that leads you up to the town.\nOnce there, place the barrel in the center of the lumber mill; someplace high, like on a crate or something.\nAfter you open it, the rest should take care of itself. Just come back here and I'll reward you for helping me.","rew":"Experience: 2,800","done":"The termites are obviously getting restless as you place the barrel on top of the crate.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":72.3,"n":"Mickey Levine","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":48.3,"y":32,"n":"Termite Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4142":{"id":4142,"t":"A Visit to Gregan","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take a Bloodpetal to Gregan Brewspewer in Feralas.\nBloodpetal Bloodpetal Lasher 80 % , Bloodpetal Flayer 80 % , Bloodpetal Thresher 80 % , Bloodpetal Trapper 80 %\nProvided: Bloodpetal","desc":"I'm not quite sure what to make of this, ‹name›. The plants... they seem to have some minimal intelligence.\nI'm no expert, though. But, I do know someone that is!\nHead to northern Feralas, and look for a buddy of mine named Gregan Brewspewer. He's an expert on this sort of thing.\nI'm sure Gregan can help us out here. You'll find him out in the wilderness; he's not the type to live in a big city.","rew":"Experience: 3,800","back":"I live out here in the forest... Peaceful.\nWell, at least I thought it would be. I get more visitors out here than I ever did when I lived in Ironforge!","done":"Bloodpetal, eh? Hmmm... Well, you better explain the plan, and then I'll tell you whether or not I can help you.\nUn'Goro Crater Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":42.9,"y":9.6,"n":"Muigin","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":45.1,"y":25.6,"n":"Gregan Brewspewer","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4382":{"id":4382,"t":"Crystal Force","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Green Power Crystal Green Power Crystal , Green Power Crystal , Mor'vek 30.8 % , Spiked Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more\n10 Blue Power Crystal Blue Power Crystal , Blue Power Crystal , Mor'vek 25.6 % , Plated Stegodon 0.3 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Crystal Force","back":"The Pylon table allows you to combine green power crystals with blue power crystals.\nAccording to J.D.'s manual, this combination can be used to increase your spirit.","done":"Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.\nThe resulting combination is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":77.2,"y":50,"n":"Eastern Crystal Pylon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4782":{"id":4782,"t":"Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe","lv":34,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Return to Menara, tell her it'll take some time, but I'll make sure to come through for her... and you. Tell her to have you finish gathering the rest of your components--I should have the thread done by then. You can return and pick it up then.\nGood luck, ‹name›. Oh, and say hello to Strahad for me while you're there. That old coot... putting a tower right there next to Ratchet... crazy.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Good, you've returned, ‹name›. And where is the thread?\nAh, I understand. That is acceptable. The goblin and his brother have not failed us yet--I suppose it is understandable that he did not have it prepared right then. So be it... we have other things we can attend to in the meantime.\nAre you prepared for the next step?\nStranglethorn Vale The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.7,"y":76.9,"n":"Xizk Goodstitch","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7582":{"id":7582,"t":"The Prison's Casing","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring and recover 5 Tears of the Hederine from the Hederine demons that occupy the gorge. Return to Daio in the Tainted Scar when you have completed this task.\n5 Tears of the Hederine Hederine Slayer 80 % , Hederine Initiate 80 % , Hederine Manastalker 80 %","desc":"The Hederine demons that occupy the foothills of Mount Hyjal secrete powerful fel poisons, which if left to mature, harden into a dense anti-magic crystal. These crystals have come to be known as Tears of the Hederine.\nNot even the immense power of a Doomguard could break the walls of a prison constructed from this material.\nTravel to Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring and recover the Tears.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"The Hederine will not give up their precious gems without a fight, ‹name›.","done":"I merely need to combine the blood of the Wildspawn with these crystals and the prison shall be ready for use.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":34.1,"y":50.1,"n":"Daio the Decrepit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1502":{"id":1502,"t":"Thun'grim Firegaze","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 210 experience instead of 200, 1.05 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens.","desc":"It is vital that a warrior's weapon is one of quality. And if there is an orc who can craft quality weapons, then that orc is Thun'grim Firegaze. He is a hermit who dwells atop the hills east of the Crossroads.\nIf you seek a weapon, warrior, then you should seek Thun'grim. To find him, first travel to the Crossroads to the west, then strike east into the hills. His camp is high on a hilltop.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"My eyes have long dried out from staring into the forge's flame, but some things I can still see. I can see you want something.\nAnd if you found your way here, then I can guess what you desire.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":61.4,"y":21.1,"n":"Uzzek","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1822":{"id":1822,"t":"Heirloom Weapon","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHeirloom Axe Heirloom Hammer Heirloom Dagger Heirloom Sword\nExperience: 875","done":"I will keep three of the weapons you returned to me, as mementos of my pain and loss. But please, ‹name›, choose your favorite of the heirlooms and keep it for yourself.\nMay it serve you greater than it served its cursed, former owners.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52.3,"n":"Coleman Farthing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5022":{"id":5022,"t":"Better Late Than Never","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Check with the Royal Factors of Stormwind to learn the whereabouts of an Emma Felstone. There is usually a census officer located in City Hall.\nJanice's Parcel\nProvided: Janice's Parcel","desc":"You pick up the package, wiping off a small layer of dust and grime that had settled on it. It is addressed in a hurried hand to an Emma Felstone of Stormwind; the delivery of the package is dated for well over four years ago.\nThough it is unclear if Emma Felstone is even alive, it is widely known that the Stormwind City Hall keep records on the populace of the city. This is handled through the Royal Factors of the Stormwind Census.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Welcome to the office of the Stormwind census. If you are in need of information on our populace, then I can assist you.","done":"A package for an Emma Felstone, you say? Last known address was Stormwind, four years ago? Well let me see here...\nAccording to what we know, there was an Emma Felstone in the city about four years ago. Well, I should say possibly - this census I refer to is from five years ago, and I don't have a report of her vacating the city. This doesn't mean that she is still here though.\nWait a second... this package couldn't be for Ol' Emma, could it?\nWestern Plaguelands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":38.7,"y":55.2,"n":"Janice's Parcel","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.2,"y":48.1,"n":"Royal Factor Bathrilor","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5342":{"id":5342,"t":"The Last Barov","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,800, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Chillwind Camp - Alliance territory - and assassinate Weldon Barov. Take his head and return to Alexi Barov.\nBe warned, Weldon will probably be well protected by Alliance scum.\nHead of Weldon Barov Weldon Barov","desc":"Naturally, with my brother still alive, there may be some contention as to the primary beneficiary of the family's fortune. This cannot be.\nA low down guttersnipe like you isn't above a little cold-blooded murder, I hope.\nIt's a simple task and one that I expect you will complete; that is, if you wish to claim your reward.\nWeldon sits under Alliance protection at Chillwind Camp, to the east. Slay him, return his head.\n<Alexi yawns.>\nHurry along now.","rew":"You will receive:\nBarov Peasant Caller\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300","back":"Secure my fortune and share in the spoils.","done":"Wonderful! Now only I hold the power and fortune of house Barov!\n<Alexi throws a large bag at you.>\nAnd keep the change, you filthy animal.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":71.6,"n":"Alexi Barov","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"142":{"id":142,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Track down the Defias Messenger in Westfall and bring his message to Stoutmantle.\nA Mysterious Message Defias Messenger","desc":"We need to discover the location of the Defias hideout. ‹name›, my scout reports that a Defias Messenger has been seen on the roads between Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry and the Jangolode Mine. I want you to capture him. If he resists, kill him and bring me whatever he is carrying.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, were you able to gather any information? Did you locate the messenger?","done":"This is indeed firm proof that VanCleef is in charge. Now all we need to know is where the Defias gang is hiding out.\nWe've had a stroke of luck while you were gone. We captured a thief trying to steal Saldean's wagon. He has promised to lead us to the hideout in exchange for his life. I want you to defend the traitor so he can reveal the hideout. Return to me once you have uncovered the location.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92462":{"id":92462,"t":"Infestation investigation","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Pesky Cirrusflies in Thendal Grove.\nPesky Cirrusfly slain : 0/ 8","desc":"One of our rangers recently reported an infestation of cirrusflies here in Thendal Grove.\nCirrusflies can be dangerous if the swarm is allowed to grow too large, so please head to the eastern end of the Grove and exterminate as many as you can.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 0 silver, 35 copper Experience: 170\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"Such pests cannot be allowed to find root in our peaceful grove. An infestation can quickly grow dangerous if left unchecked.","done":"Judging by the amount of bug entrails covering you, this must be quite the infestation.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.4,"y":24.8,"n":"Elatrell Featherlight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8142":{"id":8142,"t":"Zandalarian Shadow Talisman","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Zandalarian Shadow Talisman","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalarian Shadow Talisman\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Impressive, ‹name›. You have a gift for killing that I have not sensed in another in many years. Even Molthor is aware of the work that you have done for Zandalar. It is time to enhance your talisman further. Give it to me.","done":"There is only one enhancement left that can be placed on the talisman, ‹class›. When the time is right, I shall apply that enhancement.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});